## 4. Decision Matrix: MCP Capabilities & Enterprise Tradeoffs

Table 04.02 evaluates capability trade-offs for enterprise MCP server implementations.

| Capability Feature | Operational Benefit | Security Risk | Network Overhead | Recommended Production Baseline |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Resource Subscriptions** | Real-time context updates without polling | Memory bloat on long-lived connections | Low (Lightweight notifications) | ✅ Enable for live logs and active configs |
| **Dynamic Tool Modification** | Tools registered/deregistered at runtime | Tool confusion if schemas mutate mid-task | Low | ⚠️ Use only for modular plugin systems |
| **Client Roots Negotiation** | Informs server of workspace filesystem boundaries | Path traversal if server ignores roots | Negligible | ✅ **Mandatory** for desktop filesystem tools |
| **Server-Initiated Sampling** | Allows MCP server to query Claude recursively | Runaway token spend, recursion loops | High (Nested LLM turns) | ❌ Disable by default; gate behind quotas |

